y one place could therefore produce a correct decision with a misleading message. The refactor gives the existing pure module responsibility for selecting the first rejection reason. The form translates that reason into the same text students saw before, and existing callers still receive a Boolean from canBook. A request blocked for several reasons makes this separation observable because the first failure determines what the student sees. The fixtures all use start and end, and the checker has one booking policy. Both facts support keeping the design to one small module boundary.</p></section><h2>Verification</h2><p>The original project passed 34 tests. Before editing its implementation, four form tests were added to record the existing priority of validation messages. The same expanded suite passed all 38 tests before and after the refactor.</p><p>Run <code>npm test -- --reporter=verbose</code> inside <code>smart-campus</code>. See the <a href="evidence/01-before.txt">original run</a>, <a href="evidence/02-before-expanded.txt">expanded baseline</a>, <a href="evidence/03-after.txt">final run</a>, <a href="evidence/04-build.txt">production build</a> and <a href="evidence/05-replay.txt">mutation replay</a>.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Criterion</th><th>Coverage</th><th>Expected behavior</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>AC1 · Time validity</td><td>T02–T05, T16–T21, T24</td><td>Past, starts-now, reversed, zero-length and out-of-day requests fail. A valid request may end at 1440.</td></tr><tr><td>AC2 · Duration</td><td>T06, T07, UI06</td><td>120 minutes is allowed. 121 minutes is rejected.</td></tr><tr><td>AC3 · Blocked room</td><td>T13, UI02</td><td>An otherwise free interval is unavailable when blocked.</td></tr><tr><td>AC4 · Intersections</td><td>T01, T08–T12, T14, T22</td><td>Both touching directions are available. Partial, contained, containing and identical intersections conflict.</td></tr><tr><td>AC5 · Preservation</td><td>T15, T25, T26, UI01, UI05</td><td>The existing array keeps its values, order and references. Repeated checks show a single scheduled booking.</td></tr><tr><td>AC6 · Feedback</td><td>UI01–UI08, four new priority cases, screenshots</td><td>Rejected requests keep their original explanations. Both tested viewport widths fit without horizontal overflow.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Browser comparison</h2><p>Both versions used the same 11:00–12:00 request immediately after the existing booking. The desktop check used the unblocked room. The mobile check used the blocked room. Captured result text and page widths matched across versions.</p><aside><figure><a href="evidence/screenshots/after-desktop.jpg"><img src="evidence/screenshots/after-desktop.jpg" alt="Desktop · 1280 px · Available"></a><figcaption>Desktop · 1280 px · Available · <a href="evidence/screenshots/before-desktop.jpg">Before</a></figcaption></figure><figure><a href="evidence/screenshots/after-mobile.jpg"><img src="evidence/screenshots/after-mobile.jpg" alt="Mobile · 390 px · Unavailable"></a><figcaption>Mobile · 390 px · Unavailable · <a href="evidence/screenshots/before-mobile.jpg">Before</a></figcaption></figure></aside><h2>Changed project files</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>src/booking.js</td><td>bookingIssue returns the first rejection reason or null. canBook derives its Boolean from that single result.</td></tr><tr><td>src/App.jsx</td><td>The submit handler asks for one reason and selects the existing message. Form controls, fixture data and markup are preserved.</td></tr><tr><td>src/feedback-priority.test.jsx</td><td>Four new form tests pin the order of explanations when conditions compete. Both original test files are byte-identical to the baseline.</td></tr><tr><td>AGENTS.md</td><td>New root instructions describe the contract, project structure, scope and verification commands.</td></tr><tr><td>scripts/replay.mjs</td><td>Update the insertion point used by the previous practice’s deliberate mutation experiment. All seven replay stages were verified.</td></tr><tr><td>scripts/validate-package.mjs</td><td>Omitted from the new export. This old packaging helper checked Practice 08’s bug-detector skill and its submission folder.</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href="evidence/practice08-to-09.diff">Full before/after source diff</a></p><h2>AI review and reflection</h2><p>Both local reviews recommended one rule module. Explicitly supplying AGENTS.md made the second response name the Boolean contract, exact commands and competing failures to test. The form now contains no duration or overlap calculation. The only supporting script change keeps the earlier mutation replay working. The supplied comparison uses the same Codex session, and the original Practice 08 footer remains visible because the exercise calls for preserving the UI.</p><p>The student selected a local ZIP. The two review responses are attributed to Codex, and the working demo opens from the extracted files. A hosted Bolt link and Bolt chat transcripts would require a separate Bolt session.</p></main></html>
